            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-main mb-2">Q1: Is negative marking applicable in MPSC Prelims?</h3>
            <p class="text-text-muted m-0">A1: Yes, there is a negative marking of 1/4th (0.25) marks for every wrong answer marked in both Paper I and Paper II of the Prelims exam.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-bg-surface border border-border-card p-5 rounded-2xl">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text-main mb-2">Q2: How many attempts are allowed for general category candidates?</h3>
            <p class="text-text-muted m-0">A2: Unlike UPSC, MPSC has removed the attempt limits for state services. Candidates can appear for MPSC exams as long as they satisfy the age eligibility criteria.</p>
